Let $z = 4 - \sqrt{3} + (-1 - 4 \sqrt{3})i.$  A $120^\circ$ rotation around the origin in the clockwise direction is the same as a $240^\circ$ rotation in the counterclockwise direction.  Thus, we multiply $z$ by $\operatorname{cis} (-120^\circ) = \operatorname{cis} (240^\circ) = \cos 240^\circ + i \sin 240^\circ = -\frac{1}{2} - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} i.$  Then
\begin{align*} z \operatorname{cis} (-120^\circ) &= (4 - \sqrt{3} + (-1 - 4 \sqrt{3})i) \left( -\frac{1}{2} - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} i \right) \\ &= (4 - \sqrt{3}) \left( -\frac{1}{2} - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} i \right) + (-1 - 4 \sqrt{3})i \left( -\frac{1}{2} - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} i \right) \\ &= (4 - \sqrt{3}) \left( -\frac{1}{2} \right) + (4 - \sqrt{3}) \left( -\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} i \right) + (-1 - 4 \sqrt{3})i \left( -\frac{1}{2} \right) + (-1 - 4 \sqrt{3})i \left( -\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} i \right) \\ &= -\frac{1}{2} (4 - \sqrt{3}) - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} (4 - \sqrt{3}) i + \frac{1}{2} (1 + 4 \sqrt{3}) i + \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} (1 + 4 \sqrt{3}) i^2 \\ &= -\frac{1}{2} (4 - \sqrt{3}) - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} (1 + 4 \sqrt{3}) + \left( \frac{1}{2} (1 + 4 \sqrt{3}) - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} (4 - \sqrt{3}) \right) i \\ &= -\frac{1}{2} (4 - \sqrt{3}) - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} (1 + 4 \sqrt{3}) + \left( \frac{1}{2} + 2 \sqrt{3} - \frac{4 \sqrt{3}}{2} + \frac{3}{2} \right) i \\ &= -\frac{1}{2} (4 - \sqrt{3}) - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} (1 + 4 \sqrt{3}) + \left( \frac{1}{2} + 2 \sqrt{3} - 2 \sqrt{3} + \frac{3}{2} \right) i \\ &= -\frac{1}{2} (4 - \sqrt{3}) - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} (1 + 4 \sqrt{3}) + \left( \frac{4}{2} \right) i \\ &= -\frac{1}{2} (4 - \sqrt{3}) - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} (1 + 4 \sqrt{3}) + 2i \\ &= -2 + \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} - \frac{4 \cdot 3}{2} + 2i \\ &= -2 - \frac{12}{2} + 2i \\ &= -2 - 6 + 2i \\ &= -8 + 2i. \end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{-8 + 2i}$

